<p><b>Eustace's Bio:</b>
<table border=1 width=400>
  <tr><td>
  Someone calls?  Happy to sit for a while to talk.  Care for a drink?  A bite to eat?  Nothing, then.  Do make yourself comfortable.  Ah... relaxed, are we?  A test: Can you stand up? I didn't think so.  Panic doesn't suit you, friend.  There's nothing wrong with spending a little extra time in that chair, particularly when you haven't yet told me who you are.  I noticed the necromantic sigils on your cloak before you even entered, you see.  Yes, the cloak in your bag - but you were wearing it when you walked up the path to my home.  Surprised? If I let you leave with the memory of this conversation, look up the meaning of these two spells: "Sentinel" and "Shifting Sight".  If you're as intelligent as you act, you'll figure it out.  Few humans approach my domicile uninvited, and fewer still are as dangerous as a necromancer.  If you are truly a Bloodsaber as you say, then perhaps you will tell me of Bertoxxulus?  Of course I know the name - I serve him as well.  How did you think I weakened your bone and atrophied your muscle so easily?  Bertoxxulus teaches more than necromancy, and means more than death.  Hold your spells! Need I enthrall you to have a simple conversation?  My ways are not so different from your own.  Have a drink, you look to need it.  I first learned the way of Bertoxxulus from the lips of a Bloodsaber, Wascen Witherfist.  Then when next I visited Ak'Anon, there I met a Priest of Rust who taught the rest.  He teaches me still.  Changed your mind, hmm?  I'm no threat to the Bloodsabers - in fact, should your armies pass my way, I'll happily provide my own clarity to your necromancers and augment their walking bones.  So long as we understand each other.
  </td></tr>
</table>



